WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.619
Hi everyone. In this video, we're going to introduce CAPABLE.

00:00:08.057 --> 00:00:11.445
Consider a robot instructed to place the plate inside the drawer.

00:00:12.291 --> 00:00:19.122
A failure in one joint changes the robot's physical capability, making the intended motion difficult to execute.

00:00:21.537 --> 00:00:25.998
A pre-trained VLA policy continues producing nominal actions,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:33.166
unaware that the actual movement no longer matches what was commanded, causing the robot to deviate from its intended motion.

00:00:36.115 --> 00:00:43.649
CAPABLE addresses this problem by inferring the robot's current capability from its joint-execution history and kinematic structure.

00:00:44.435 --> 00:00:50.276
A residual policy then adapts the frozen VLA action to the robot's altered dynamics.

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.273
The system receives the visual observation and language instruction.

00:00:56.849 --> 00:01:00.621
The frozen OpenVLA OFT generates the nominal action chunk.

00:01:01.041 --> 00:01:06.488
In parallel, CAPABLE maintains a sixteen-step history of commanded and observed joint motions,

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:11.991
capturing discrepancies between intended and actual execution.

00:01:12.786 --> 00:01:20.485
A shared temporal encoder processes each joint independently, enabling generalization to unseen actuator failures.

00:01:21.889 --> 00:01:27.601
The joint representations are combined with the robot configuration, Jacobian, and nominal action.

00:01:29.137 --> 00:01:32.827
Cross-joint attention captures interactions between joint capabilities.

00:01:33.502 --> 00:01:40.629
These features form a capability latent that conditions the residual policy through feature-wise modulation.

00:01:42.029 --> 00:01:46.110
The residual policy generates a correction to the nominal VLA action.

00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:52.982
The corrected action is executed, and the resulting joint feedback updates the capability estimate.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:02:04.981
CAPABLE thus enables online adaptation to unseen actuator failures without fault labels, joint identifiers, or reference trajectories.

00:02:06.395 --> 00:02:07.230
Thank you for watching.
